VERDICT: PASS -- the one copper link came back after all 18 flaps. 9 flaps were on the DUT
         and 9 on the 4050, 3 at each of auto 1000, auto 100 and auto 10. Each time the link
         came back at full duplex and the set speed in 2.8-4.5 s.
  Method (the database has no steps): flap the link with shutdown and then no shutdown.
  Do it 3 times at each speed, from each end. Set the speed on the DUT with
  `speed auto <n>`. The 4050 stays at auto. Expected after each flap: the port reads
  "connected" at full duplex and the set speed. The Link Layer Discovery Protocol (LLDP)
  neighbour comes back. The DUT log shows one "Port down" line and one "Port up" line.
      local flaps (on the DUT) ..... 9 of 9 back at a-full and the set speed  (4.5 s at auto 1000,
                                     2.8 s at auto 100 and auto 10)
      remote flaps (on the 4050) ... 9 of 9 back at a-full and the set speed  (2.8 s each)
      down after shutdown .......... 18 of 18  ("disabled" at the first status read, 1.2 s)
