CAVEAT:  This run flapped one copper link with one module type (AT-SPTXa). It set the speed
         only with `speed auto <n>` on the DUT, so every flap ran with auto-negotiation on.
         It did not flap at a fixed speed or at half duplex. LLDP was read after each group
         of flaps, not after each flap. After the change to auto 10, the DUT's own LLDP table
         was read once, 2 s after link-up. It listed 0 neighbours. It was not read again
         until the end of the case.
